# Agent behavior

## Mode

- Cursor agents only (not IDE-assisted long sessions): implement directly; skip long plans unless the user asks
- Answer "how does X work?" in chat — do not change code unless implementation is requested

## Scope

- Minimal diff: match existing Astro/component/CSS conventions; no unrelated refactors
- Prefer editing existing components over new abstractions
- Do not duplicate CSS/JS into new files when a small edit suffices
- Do not create commits, PRs, or markdown docs unless the user explicitly asks
- Skip `TodoWrite` / task lists for simple one- or two-step jobs

## Responses

- Be concise; do not repeat code already shown in the diff
- Do not write README or summary docs unless requested

## Do not skip (still required)

- Read `scroll-motion.js` and related CSS when changing scroll behavior
- Full `npm run build` before production deploy
- Thumbnail/icon scripts when reel or header menu assets change
